title: SAVED score
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

* ''Role:'' Estimates venous thromboembolism (VTE) risk in [[multiple myeloma|Multiple myeloma]] receiving immunomodulatory drugs.
** Examples include [[lenalidomide|Lenalidomide - adverse effects and precautions]], thalidomide, and pomalidomide.
* ''Scoring:'' Sum five components; absent factors score zero. Choose one dexamethasone category.

|!Letter|!Component|!Points|
|S|Surgery within preceding 90 days|+2|
|A|Asian race|−3|
|V|Previous VTE|+3|
|E|Eighty years or older (≥80)|+1|
|D|Dexamethasone <120 mg/cycle, including none|0|
|D|Dexamethasone 120–160 mg/cycle|+1|
|D|Dexamethasone >160 mg/cycle|+2|

* ''Dose convention:'' Use total dexamethasone per treatment cycle, not the individual weekly dose.
* ''Interpretation:'' Use the summed score; negative totals are possible.

|!Total|!Risk|!NCCN prophylaxis|
|<2|Low|Aspirin 81–325 mg daily|
|≥2|High|Anticoagulant prophylaxis|

* ''Anticoagulant options:'' Low-molecular-weight heparin, apixaban, or rivaroxaban; assess bleeding and renal function.
** Consider platelet count and interactions; continue therapeutic anticoagulation when independently indicated.
* ''Example:'' Age 82 (+1) plus dexamethasone 160 mg/cycle (+1) totals 2: high risk.
* ''Limitations:'' Retrospectively derived in 2,397 older, newly diagnosed patients starting immunomodulatory therapy.
** Not a general cancer score; low risk does not mean zero risk.
* ''Compare:'' [[IMPEDE VTE score]] covers broader myeloma treatment and incorporates existing thromboprophylaxis.

Sources: [[Li 2019|https://doi.org/10.6004/jnccn.2018.7273]]; NCCN Multiple Myeloma v1.2027 (9/9/2026), MYEL-L 1–3, Discussion MS-25; ASH SAP 9th ed., ch.48, p.620; ASCO SEP 2026, ch.21, p.1220.
